WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
Carnation Evaporated Milk presents the George Burns and Gracie Allen Show.

00:31.000 --> 00:32.000
Hello, Harry.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
Oh, Gracie. I've been looking for you all over. I've got Blanchard's Christmas presents here.

00:36.000 --> 00:37.000
Oh, Gracie.

00:37.000 --> 00:38.000
Will you hide them for me?

00:38.000 --> 00:39.000
What is it?

00:39.000 --> 00:42.000
Oh, I got her a red alligator bag and shoes to match.

00:42.000 --> 00:47.000
Oh, it's lovely, Harry. But I always thought alligators were brown.

00:48.000 --> 00:49.000
It's dyed.

00:49.000 --> 00:53.000
Oh, well, I hope it has, if they made a bag and shoes out of it.

00:55.000 --> 00:57.000
Look, Gracie, where can I hide these?

00:57.000 --> 00:59.000
Oh, well, I'll put them in the clothes rack.

00:59.000 --> 01:00.000
I'll be back here.

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
Gracie, is that you out there?

01:02.000 --> 01:03.000
Yes, Blanche.

01:03.000 --> 01:05.000
Look, Gracie, I'll hide them. You talk to Blanche.

01:05.000 --> 01:06.000
Oh, all right.

01:06.000 --> 01:10.000
Oh, and remember, shh. You haven't seen me.

01:10.000 --> 01:11.000
Oh, shh.

01:16.000 --> 01:17.000
Hi, honey.

01:17.000 --> 01:18.000
Hi, Blanche.

01:18.000 --> 01:19.000
Oh, hi, Blanche.

01:20.000 --> 01:21.000
Who are you talking to?

01:21.000 --> 01:23.000
Well, it could have been Harry. I haven't seen him.

01:25.000 --> 01:26.000
What?

01:26.000 --> 01:29.000
Say, Blanche, will you go to the train with me today?

01:29.000 --> 01:32.000
Maybe Kelly and her three children are arriving in about an hour.

01:32.000 --> 01:35.000
Oh, sure. They're going to spend the holidays with you.

01:35.000 --> 01:38.000
Yes. And George is so happy.

01:39.000 --> 01:40.000
George is happy?

01:40.000 --> 01:41.000
Well, he must be.

01:41.000 --> 01:46.000
He said, with 30 million homes in this country, just my luck they're coming here.

01:50.000 --> 01:53.000
Well, anyway, having children around the holidays,

01:53.000 --> 01:56.000
I think it's the only thing in my whole...

01:56.000 --> 01:57.000
What's that for?

01:57.000 --> 01:59.000
Oh, you blanched Harry.

02:03.000 --> 02:04.000
Oh, hello, Harry.

02:04.000 --> 02:08.000
Hi. I was inside talking to George.

02:08.000 --> 02:09.000
Oh, you were?

02:09.000 --> 02:11.000
Yes, I was. So help me, I was.

02:11.000 --> 02:13.000
If you don't believe me, ask Gracie. Wasn't I Gracie?

02:13.000 --> 02:16.000
Well, better yet, ask George. He'll be home in a few minutes.

02:20.000 --> 02:22.000
I got tired of waiting for him.

02:22.000 --> 02:28.000
Oh, Harry, Gracie and I are going down to the station to meet Mamie Kelly and her three children.

02:28.000 --> 02:31.000
Why don't you come along and help us carry the luggage?

02:31.000 --> 02:35.000
Mamie Kelly and her three children, when they were here before, they kicked me?

02:35.000 --> 02:38.000
They, they, they, they, they, they shot out the window of that door?

02:38.000 --> 02:41.000
Oh, yes, Harry. I'm glad you remembered them.

02:43.000 --> 02:45.000
Well, I will not help with their luggage.

02:45.000 --> 02:46.000
Oh, yes, you will.

02:46.000 --> 02:52.000
No, I won't.

02:55.000 --> 02:57.000
Well, I won't.

03:07.000 --> 03:10.000
Well, only two more days to do your shopping.

03:10.000 --> 03:13.000
Of course, the smart people are all through.

03:13.000 --> 03:16.000
Only dopes wait until now.

03:16.000 --> 03:18.000
You'd be surprised how many dopes there are.

03:19.000 --> 03:21.000
Thought I'd never get out of that store today.

03:23.000 --> 03:26.000
I went shopping with Gracie. It was quite an experience.

03:26.000 --> 03:32.000
We were standing in line having a gift wrap, and Gracie fell into a conversation with this woman in front of her.

03:32.000 --> 03:36.000
And, well, I shouldn't say that she fell in, she jumped in.

03:37.000 --> 03:40.000
You see, nobody is a stranger to Gracie.

03:40.000 --> 03:43.000
She loves to talk to people that she's never seen before.

03:44.000 --> 03:47.000
Which makes it nice because they're the people who talk to her.

03:49.000 --> 03:55.000
Anyway, this woman said that she was visiting here from New York State and that her husband ran a Buffalo newspaper.

03:55.000 --> 03:58.000
And Gracie says, that's wonderful. How did he teach him to read?

04:01.000 --> 04:04.000
And then before I knew it, she was talking to some other woman.

04:04.000 --> 04:10.000
And this woman was buying gloves for her children to give to their teachers for Christmas.

04:10.000 --> 04:14.000
And she told Gracie that she hoped that they wouldn't be too tight.

04:14.000 --> 04:18.000
And Gracie said, well, if they are, why don't you wait until they sober up?

04:23.000 --> 04:26.000
You know, in about 20 minutes we had that counter all to ourselves.

04:29.000 --> 04:32.000
As I said, shopping with Gracie is quite an experience.

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
I wouldn't go through that again for $8.75.

04:35.000 --> 04:39.000
The expression used to be, I wouldn't go through that again for $1,000.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.000
But I'm figuring it after taxes.

04:45.000 --> 04:47.000
Another thing happened in the store.

04:47.000 --> 04:49.000
Oh, our Christmas guests are arriving.

04:49.000 --> 05:04.000
Yeah, that's them. Lud, a little entrance music.

05:04.000 --> 05:21.000
Oh, Mamey!

05:21.000 --> 05:25.000
Mamey, you did it. You did it, Mamey. One of my good cigars.

05:25.000 --> 05:29.000
Oh, Gracie, the house looks so nice and creepy.

05:29.000 --> 05:32.000
Do you think so, Mamey? I just got that brief today.

05:32.000 --> 05:35.000
Do you like it?

05:35.000 --> 05:37.000
Hello, hello.

05:37.000 --> 05:40.000
Okay, okay, I hope you did it too.

05:40.000 --> 05:43.000
There it is. Another one.

05:43.000 --> 05:46.000
Let's see. Let's see where you all go.

05:46.000 --> 05:49.000
Let's see where you want to go.

05:49.000 --> 05:51.000
Yeah, we're done.

05:51.000 --> 05:53.000
Thank you, Harry. That was wonderful.

05:53.000 --> 05:57.000
Now, I was just saying, I want to see where everybody's going to sleep.

05:57.000 --> 06:01.000
You three children can have the front bed.

06:01.000 --> 06:06.000
Mamey, you and I will sleep in our bedroom.

06:06.000 --> 06:08.000
I don't want to crowd George out of his bed.

06:08.000 --> 06:10.000
Oh, he won't be in it.

06:13.000 --> 06:15.000
Joe is coming on the later train, Gracie.

06:15.000 --> 06:17.000
Yes, we'll take the stair room, don't you worry.

06:17.000 --> 06:20.000
Oh, all right. Well, then that settles everything.

06:20.000 --> 06:23.000
Everybody is settled except Blanche and Harry.

06:25.000 --> 06:29.000
Gracie, we live next door. Maybe we could sleep over there.

06:29.000 --> 06:32.000
Oh, that's a wonderful idea.

06:32.000 --> 06:34.000
Well, that's about it.

06:34.000 --> 06:36.000
Yes.

06:36.000 --> 06:38.000
Look, Harry, will you bring the things upstairs, please?

06:38.000 --> 06:40.000
With George standing right there?

06:40.000 --> 06:43.000
Oh, George will go first.

06:49.000 --> 06:51.000
Harry, I'll take it. I'll leave it out.

06:51.000 --> 06:53.000
Thank you. Thank you so much.

06:53.000 --> 06:55.000
Thank you so much.

06:55.000 --> 06:57.000
What is it?

06:57.000 --> 07:00.000
George, can we go out and play?

07:00.000 --> 07:02.000
Joe, can we go out and play?

07:02.000 --> 07:04.000
I don't know. Mother, can we go out and play?

07:04.000 --> 07:06.000
Gracie, is it all right if the children go out and play?

07:06.000 --> 07:09.000
George, is it all right if the children go out and play?

07:12.000 --> 07:14.000
Wait, I'll call my agent.

07:19.000 --> 07:22.000
Yes, now be very careful going up the stairs.

07:22.000 --> 07:24.000
Don't get me. Don't get me.

07:24.000 --> 07:27.000
Oh, Mamie, I'm so glad you could come down for Christmas.

07:27.000 --> 07:30.000
I am, June. I have so many things to tell you.

07:30.000 --> 07:33.000
Oh, wonderful. Well, while you're telling, I'll get some coffee.

07:33.000 --> 07:35.000
Yes.

07:35.000 --> 07:37.000
Oh, wait a minute. You get it.

07:37.000 --> 07:39.000
I'll sit there so I won't miss anything.

07:39.000 --> 07:41.000
Oh, you'll never change.

07:41.000 --> 07:44.000
Oh, you'll never change.

07:44.000 --> 07:47.000
Well, I'll get the coffee.

07:47.000 --> 07:49.000
Oh, George.

07:49.000 --> 07:51.000
I have some Christmas presents in that big grip.

07:51.000 --> 07:53.000
Will you bring it down?

07:53.000 --> 07:55.000
Okay, Mamie.

07:55.000 --> 07:58.000
Oh, Mamie, I'm just dying to hear what you have to tell me.

07:58.000 --> 08:00.000
Well, of course.

08:00.000 --> 08:02.000
There you go.

08:02.000 --> 08:04.000
No, no, no, George. That's not the grip.

08:04.000 --> 08:06.000
You said the big one.

08:06.000 --> 08:08.000
Well, I meant the other big one.

08:08.000 --> 08:10.000
Well, the other big one is smaller than this big one.

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
That's what it is.

08:12.000 --> 08:14.000
Is that the one?

08:14.000 --> 08:16.000
Mamie, a carnation.

08:16.000 --> 08:18.000
Oh, I love it.

08:18.000 --> 08:21.000
Say, Gracie, did you read in the paper where a carnation bull won the first prize of this livestock show?

08:21.000 --> 08:24.000
Yes, and they certainly must have had men judges.

08:24.000 --> 08:27.000
The cows give all the milk and the bull gets the blue ribbon.

08:32.000 --> 08:34.000
It's a man's world, all right.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.000
Yes, it certainly is.

08:36.000 --> 08:38.000
Doctor, here I am again.

08:38.000 --> 08:40.000
Mamie, Mamie.

08:38.000 --> 08:40.000
Just put it right there.

08:40.000 --> 08:42.000
There it is.

08:42.000 --> 08:44.000
Oh, good.

08:44.000 --> 08:46.000
Oh, I haven't called for you.

08:46.000 --> 08:48.000
No, you were right the first time. It is the other grip.

08:48.000 --> 08:50.000
I thought so.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.000
Why didn't you bring that time?

08:52.000 --> 08:54.000
I'm breaking in these shoes for a friend.

08:54.000 --> 08:56.000
Oh.

08:56.000 --> 08:58.000
Gracie, Mamie,

08:58.000 --> 09:00.000
tell me all of you, how's everybody in Sabaton?

09:00.000 --> 09:02.000
Oh, fine.

09:02.000 --> 09:04.000
I ran into your Uncle Fred the other day.

09:04.000 --> 09:06.000
Oh, did you? How is he?

09:06.000 --> 09:08.000
Good. Why didn't he ever marry Millie McGrath?

09:08.000 --> 09:11.000
Well, she wouldn't marry him as long as he kept drinking.

09:11.000 --> 09:13.000
He wouldn't stop?

09:13.000 --> 09:15.000
Oh, sure, but when he got sober, he wouldn't marry her.

09:17.000 --> 09:19.000
I'll never forget the Christmas party.

09:19.000 --> 09:21.000
I'll never forget the Christmas that he gave me.

09:21.000 --> 09:23.000
Okay, here we come again.

09:23.000 --> 09:25.000
Oh, good.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.000
Show them all that, baby.

09:27.000 --> 09:29.000
Awfully nice.

09:29.000 --> 09:31.000
Hey, look at this. Christmas.

09:31.000 --> 09:33.000
Christmas.

09:33.000 --> 09:35.000
Hey, Gracie, I noticed you don't have your Christmas tree up.

09:35.000 --> 09:37.000
Now, where are we going to put the presents?

09:37.000 --> 09:39.000
Oh, I see.

09:39.000 --> 09:41.000
How about upstairs?

09:41.000 --> 09:43.000
Oh, yes.

09:43.000 --> 09:45.000
Come on.

09:45.000 --> 09:47.000
Come on.

09:47.000 --> 09:49.000
Oh, hey.

09:49.000 --> 09:51.000
What is it?

09:51.000 --> 09:53.000
Where is it?

09:53.000 --> 09:55.000
Oh, you're not getting it.

09:55.000 --> 09:57.000
What is this?

09:57.000 --> 09:59.000
Oh, that's George's sweater.

09:59.000 --> 10:01.000
Oh, you're just pulling it all out of shape.

10:01.000 --> 10:03.000
Now, go on upstairs and get cleaned up.

10:03.000 --> 10:05.000
The very idea.

10:05.000 --> 10:07.000
Oh, look what they did.

10:07.000 --> 10:09.000
Well, Mamie, don't worry about it.

10:09.000 --> 10:11.000
I'll put arm holes in this pot

10:11.000 --> 10:25.000
and he can wear it for long under his.

10:25.000 --> 10:29.000
Well, how do you like the way Gracie's going to fix my sweater?

10:29.000 --> 10:31.000
You know, that kind of thinking runs in her family.

10:31.000 --> 10:35.000
Ever tell you the business her father and uncle were in?

10:35.000 --> 10:37.000
Her father used to saw barrels and halves

10:37.000 --> 10:39.000
and then sell the halves to her uncle

10:39.000 --> 10:41.000
as wooden tubs.

10:41.000 --> 10:43.000
And her uncle would glue the halves together

10:43.000 --> 10:49.000
and sell them to her father for barrels.

10:49.000 --> 10:51.000
Now, don't laugh.

10:51.000 --> 10:53.000
They picked up $25 a piece a week for years.

10:53.000 --> 10:55.000
Of course, they had to go to the unemployment office

10:55.000 --> 10:57.000
to pick it up.

10:57.000 --> 10:59.000
See, the barrel business didn't make...

10:59.000 --> 11:01.000
Oh, a little confusion.

11:01.000 --> 11:03.000
Oh, yes, because I'm a Georgian.

11:03.000 --> 11:05.000
Just a minute.

11:05.000 --> 11:07.000
Now, wait a minute.

11:07.000 --> 11:09.000
Now, I like drum music just as much as anybody,

11:09.000 --> 11:11.000
but, well, not all day.

11:11.000 --> 11:13.000
And besides, if you keep pounding on the drum,

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
you'll spoil the candy that's inside.

11:15.000 --> 11:17.000
Candy?

11:17.000 --> 11:19.000
Come on, let's open it.

11:19.000 --> 11:21.000
Yes!

11:21.000 --> 11:23.000
Oh, Harry, you know,

11:23.000 --> 11:25.000
I've never seen the children so happy.

11:25.000 --> 11:27.000
What happened?

11:27.000 --> 11:29.000
Well, they've gone to bust open the drum

11:29.000 --> 11:31.000
to get the candy that I told them was inside it.

11:31.000 --> 11:35.000
Oh, Harry, Morton, you should be ashamed of yourself.

11:35.000 --> 11:37.000
You know Mamie doesn't want them to eat between meals.

11:41.000 --> 11:43.000
What's the use?

11:43.000 --> 11:45.000
Oh, Harry,

11:45.000 --> 11:47.000
I put your lunch on a tray in the den.

11:47.000 --> 11:49.000
Oh, fine.

11:55.000 --> 11:57.000
Can I hide this in your house?

11:57.000 --> 11:59.000
Well, sure, what is it?

11:59.000 --> 12:01.000
It's a Christmas present for Harry.

12:01.000 --> 12:03.000
It's a fishing creel.

12:03.000 --> 12:05.000
It's a fish...

12:05.000 --> 12:07.000
I'll show you.

12:07.000 --> 12:09.000
See, it's a basket.

12:09.000 --> 12:11.000
Keep fish in.

12:11.000 --> 12:13.000
Oh, well, it's very pretty,

12:13.000 --> 12:15.000
but you should have brought a bowl.

12:15.000 --> 12:17.000
This will never hold water.

12:17.000 --> 12:19.000
No, no, honey,

12:19.000 --> 12:21.000
you don't put water in this.

12:21.000 --> 12:23.000
You see, this is for dead fish.

12:23.000 --> 12:25.000
Oh? Well, this way.

12:25.000 --> 12:27.000
It's your house.

12:29.000 --> 12:31.000
No, honey, you see, when Harry...

12:31.000 --> 12:33.000
Oh, well, let's lunch.

12:37.000 --> 12:39.000
If you're trying to get rid of me,

12:39.000 --> 12:41.000
why don't you shoot me instead of trying to starve me to death?

12:41.000 --> 12:43.000
What's that?

12:43.000 --> 12:45.000
What's what?

12:47.000 --> 12:49.000
That.

12:49.000 --> 12:51.000
Oh, that. It's a Christmas present for George.

12:51.000 --> 12:53.000
Oh, really, Frank?

12:53.000 --> 12:55.000
I thought it was for Harry.

12:57.000 --> 12:59.000
No, Gracie,

12:59.000 --> 13:01.000
it's the Christmas present you bought for George, remember?

13:01.000 --> 13:03.000
Yes.

13:03.000 --> 13:05.000
Oh, yes, yes.

13:05.000 --> 13:07.000
Now I remember.

13:11.000 --> 13:13.000
What is it, Gracie?

13:13.000 --> 13:15.000
Uh, guess.

13:17.000 --> 13:19.000
Could be anything.

13:19.000 --> 13:21.000
That's what it is.

13:21.000 --> 13:23.000
Oh, and George has wanted one

13:23.000 --> 13:29.000
for a long time.

13:29.000 --> 13:31.000
Harry?

13:31.000 --> 13:33.000
Harry, how would you like to spend Christmas

13:33.000 --> 13:35.000
with my mother and father?

13:39.000 --> 13:41.000
Don't you dare think a thing like that

13:41.000 --> 13:43.000
with your father.

13:45.000 --> 13:47.000
Besides, you always enjoyed

13:47.000 --> 13:49.000
my mother's cooking.

13:49.000 --> 13:51.000
Are you kidding?

13:51.000 --> 13:53.000
My mother, no tramp has ever come back

13:53.000 --> 13:55.000
for a second meal.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.000
Oh, I suppose

13:57.000 --> 13:59.000
your mother is a good cook.

13:59.000 --> 14:01.000
She certainly is.

14:01.000 --> 14:03.000
She even cans her own food.

14:03.000 --> 14:05.000
She has to. It's the only way the garbage man

14:05.000 --> 14:07.000
will accept it.

14:07.000 --> 14:09.000
Look, Frank, we are not going...

14:11.000 --> 14:13.000
Hey, wait a minute.

14:13.000 --> 14:21.000
Wait a minute.

14:21.000 --> 14:23.000
Where did you get those red shoes

14:23.000 --> 14:25.000
and that bag?

14:25.000 --> 14:27.000
I found them in the closet.

14:27.000 --> 14:29.000
You shouldn't do that. They...

14:29.000 --> 14:31.000
Well, they might be somebody's Christmas present.

14:31.000 --> 14:33.000
Oh, Harry, don't be absurd.

14:33.000 --> 14:35.000
Who'd want an outfit like that?

14:39.000 --> 14:41.000
Thanks.

14:41.000 --> 14:43.000
There wasn't any candy in this drum,

14:43.000 --> 14:45.000
and now we can't play it.

14:45.000 --> 14:47.000
Well, play something else.

14:47.000 --> 14:49.000
Let's play Follow the Leader.

14:49.000 --> 14:51.000
Okay. Poke the elephant.

14:51.000 --> 14:53.000
Poke the elephant. Poke the elephant.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.000
Out!

15:01.000 --> 15:03.000
Well, anyway, we are not going to your father's

15:03.000 --> 15:05.000
and mother's for Christmas.

15:05.000 --> 15:07.000
Good.

15:07.000 --> 15:09.000
They're coming here.

15:09.000 --> 15:11.000
You wouldn't believe how many of them

15:11.000 --> 15:13.000
I'll get sleep with your birthday present.

15:13.000 --> 15:15.000
They're coming.

15:15.000 --> 15:17.000
Okay.

15:25.000 --> 15:27.000
Who do you think is going to play Santa Claus

15:27.000 --> 15:29.000
for the Kelly Kids' Christmas Eve?

15:29.000 --> 15:31.000
You know, it's a shame that they can't have

15:31.000 --> 15:33.000
a white Christmas like I had

15:33.000 --> 15:35.000
back East when I was a kid.

15:35.000 --> 15:37.000
They'd get up Christmas morning,

15:37.000 --> 15:39.400
What New York is pretty around Christmas time,

15:39.400 --> 15:40.640
take Central Park.

15:40.640 --> 15:42.640
Trees covered with snow and icicles

15:42.640 --> 15:45.040
and the lake frozen over and the children skating.

15:45.040 --> 15:46.740
It's real nice.

15:46.740 --> 15:47.740
Out here, what do you do?

15:47.740 --> 15:49.940
You go to Palm Springs, sit around a pool.

15:49.940 --> 15:51.380
Who do you see?

15:51.380 --> 15:55.580
Betty Grable, Ava Gardner, Rita Hayworth.

15:55.580 --> 15:58.620
All in swimming suits.

15:58.620 --> 16:01.020
And what I'd give to see an icicle again.

16:01.020 --> 16:07.740
Oh, that's Harry Bonzell with my Santa Clause outfit.

16:07.740 --> 16:08.740
Excuse me.

16:08.740 --> 16:09.740
Come in.

16:09.740 --> 16:10.740
Harry!

16:10.740 --> 16:11.740
Hi, George.

16:11.740 --> 16:12.740
Hell, am I.

16:12.740 --> 16:13.740
I guess you know this package is for you.

16:13.740 --> 16:14.740
Oh, and she's pretty too, isn't she?

16:14.740 --> 16:15.740
This package here.

16:15.740 --> 16:16.740
I know it's this package.

16:16.740 --> 16:17.740
This is Julie Lorenz, George.

16:17.740 --> 16:18.740
She's the second daughter of the Duke of York.

16:18.740 --> 16:19.740
Oh, hello, Mr. Duke of York.

16:19.740 --> 16:20.740
This is the first time I see you, Mr. Duke of York.

16:20.740 --> 16:21.740
I'm Dr. George.

16:21.740 --> 16:22.740
I'm a professor of medicine.

16:22.740 --> 16:23.740
And I'm Dr. George.

